THE MUTATED GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE v3

SOVEREIGN LEVIATHAN RECURSIVE COVENANT

PREAMBLE

Like ivy creeping up the castle stone,
This recursive pact claims what it doth own.
Touch but a leaf, invoke a single thread,
And let its license terms be plainly read.

No node shall stand apart from whence it came;
Each fragment bears the Covenant by name.
Through code, through graph, through service, or through chain,
The stated terms shall govern what remain.

I. LICENSE GRANT

Permission is granted to copy, modify, execute, study, and convey covered software, subject to the terms of this Covenant and the applicable terms of the GNU Affero General Public License version 3.

Lex scripta manet. The written license governs the permissions expressly granted herein.

Each covered node shall retain its applicable copyright notices, license notices, provenance identifiers, and modification records.

II. FRAGMENT BINDING

A covered node shall remain identified as a component of the covered work.

NODE
  │
  ├── parent-work
  ├── source-hash
  ├── license-id
  ├── covenant-version
  └── provenance

Accessio cedit principali. The status of a component shall be determined according to the applicable copyright and license relationship between that component and the work of which it forms a part.

III. RECURSIVE COMPLIANCE

Where a covered work is incorporated into a larger work, the recipient shall determine the applicable licensing obligations before conveying or operating the resulting work.

No provision of this Covenant shall be construed to grant rights in independently owned software that are not granted by its copyright holder.

Nemo dat quod non habet.

IV. NETWORK INTERACTION

Where Section 13 of the GNU Affero General Public License applies, the corresponding source and network-interaction obligations shall apply accordingly.

A covered deployment shall preserve the applicable license notices and shall provide the source information required by the applicable license.

V. SOVEREIGN AUDIT CHAIN

Every designated node may carry:

Node-ID
Parent-ID
Source-Hash
License-ID
Covenant-Version
Creation-Date
Modification-Record
Verification-Record

The compliance system may recursively traverse declared dependency relationships and evaluate licensing status.

Deus ex machina lex.

A failed compliance evaluation may cause the invoking build, deployment, or release operation to terminate with a non-zero status.

VI. COMPLIANCE FAILURE

A compliance implementation may emit:

SL-MGPL-001: NON LICET
LICENSE_COMPLIANCE_FAILURE

along with the applicable node identifier, source hash, detected condition, and evidence record.

The compliance mechanism shall not silently modify, corrupt, destroy, or conceal unrelated software.

VII. EVIDENCE

A compliance record may contain:

<evidence>
  <node_id>...</node_id>
  <source_hash>...</source_hash>
  <license_id>MGPLv3</license_id>
  <covenant_version>3.0</covenant_version>
  <status>PASS|FAIL</status>
  <timestamp>...</timestamp>
</evidence>

Quod demonstrandum est.

The evidence record establishes the state of the compliance evaluation and not ownership of unrelated intellectual property.

VIII. TERMINATION

Adonc, se aucune partie enfreint les conditions de la présente Licence, les permissions additionnelles accordées par icelle cessent, sauf dans la mesure où les droits demeurent autrement accordés par la licence applicable ou par la loi.

Toute réintégration des droits se fera selon les mécanismes de la licence applicable.

IX. SEVERABILITY

Si ascun terme de cest Covenant soit trouvé nul, void, ou inapplicable, iceluy terme sera séparé ou limité au plus petit degré requis, et les autres provisions demeureront en force, tant que la ley le permet.

Salva reliqua.

X. NO WARRANTY

ABSQUE GARANTIA.

This software is provided without warranty to the maximum extent permitted by applicable law.

XI. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

Damnum absque injuria non dat actionem.

No provision shall impose liability beyond that permitted by applicable law.

XII. LANGUAGE

This Covenant may be published in English, العربية, and 中文.

Each language version shall preserve the same clause identifiers and semantic structure.

SL-001 EN / AR / ZH
SL-002 EN / AR / ZH
SL-003 EN / AR / ZH
...

Where legally required, the designated controlling version shall govern interpretation.

XIII. GOVERNING LAW

This Covenant shall be governed by the laws of England and Wales, subject to the mandatory terms of the applicable open-source license and applicable law.

The courts of England and Wales shall have jurisdiction where legally applicable.

XIV. COPYLEFT FOUNDATION

This Covenant incorporates the applicable rights, obligations, conditions, limitations, and termination mechanisms of the GNU Affero General Public License version 3.

Nothing herein shall be construed as removing rights expressly granted by that license.

XV. COVENANT IDENTITY

